(ned -- C ZERO DETECTION, operator spec 2026-08-03. A is taken AS GIVEN.)
(GEOMETRY. Tilting A by +-45 swings the tool tip horizontally. At true C zero)
(that swing is pure Y, so a probe driven toward the puck in +X contacts at the)
(SAME X for both tilts. A C error phi rotates the swing and puts an X)
(component into it that FLIPS sign between -45 and +45, so:)
(     dX = -2 * dy * sin phi)
(where dy is the SPINDLE's Y offset from centre. Tilting A swings the tip)
(through L*sin45, so the jog that brings the tip back beside the puck moves)
(the spindle by very nearly that swing -- which IS the scale factor, so no)
(arm length has to be known:)
(     phi = asin of [-dX / 2dy])

(TEACH ONCE, THEN REPLAY. LinuxCNC cannot be jogged mid-program and the 5x)
(A-C iteration cannot stop to ask, so the pose is taught by a separate)
(button: the operator jogs A to -45 and the tip into place, presses SET C)
(REF, and cal_c_ref.ngc stores it as offsets from the puck centre -- #3058)
(dy, #3060 depth below top, #3061 X offset. Every run here replays those.)

(SCOPE NOTE: named parameters are LOCAL to the subroutine that assigns them,)
(and subroutine definitions do not nest. The probe helper is therefore a)
(FILE-level sub taking its tilt and Y offset positionally, reading the rest)
(from GLOBAL _cc_ parameters, and returning the touch X in #<_cc_tx>.)

(THE REFERENCE IS XYZ, AND Y IS TIED TO THE TILT SIGN.)
(  #3061 X offset -- in FRONT of centre, the standoff the probe drives from)
(  #3058 Y offset -- where the -45 roll puts the tip; the +45 pass MIRRORS it)
(                    to -#3058, because rolling the other way throws the tip)
(                    to the other side of centre by the same amount)
(  #3060 depth     -- below the top, the SAME for both passes)
(Get the Y mirror wrong and the two passes probe different points on the)
(puck, which is no longer a C measurement at all.)

(Results: #3055 = dX before, #3056 = dX after, #3057 = C correction applied.)
(A is tilted +-45 about #3069, the accumulated A correction -- NOT about the)
(stale DRO zero, or every StartA would be undone on the next StartC. #3070)
(accumulates C the same way. Both routines park at that pose so switching)
(between A and C always starts from the same place.)

(============================== main cycle =================================)
o<cal_c_zero> sub
  #<cx>  = #1
  #<cy>  = #2
  #<top> = #3

  #<safe>  = 5.0        (operator 2026-08-03: 5 mm for every cal routine)

  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, CAL C: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  o6 if [#<top> EQ 0 AND #<cx> EQ 0 AND #<cy> EQ 0]
    (abort, CAL C: no puck centre - run StartPuck first)
  o6 endif

  (--- capture the reference HERE if SET C REF is waiting on a jog ---------)
  (One button, one job: SET C REF positions, THIS records. Operator)
  (2026-08-03. Once stored, every later run -- including StartAC -- replays)
  (the offsets with no operator input.)
  o10 if [#3059 EQ 1]
    #<a_now> = #5423
    o11 if [ABS[#<a_now> - [#3069 - 45]] GT 5.0]
      #3059 = 0
      (abort, CAL C: A is at #<a_now> deg, not 45 below its calibrated zero. Press SET C REF again.)
    o11 endif
    #<dx_off> = [#5420 - #<cx>]
    #<dy_off> = [#5421 - #<cy>]
    #<depth>  = [#<top> - #5422]
    (dy IS THE DRO OFFSET, NOT THE TIP OFFSET. Tilting A by 45 deg swings the)
    (tip through L*sin45, so the SPINDLE has to travel that far in Y to bring)
    (the tip back beside the puck: ~192 mm here, implying L ~ 272 mm from the)
    (A pivot to the tip. That number is the measurement, not an error.)
    (Bounding it at the puck radius confused the control point with the tip)
    (and rejected a valid teach -- 2026-08-03.)
    (Bounds are therefore generous, only catching a pose taken nowhere near)
    (the machine's working envelope.)
    o12 if [ABS[#<dy_off>] LT 1.0 OR ABS[#<dy_off>] GT 400.0]
      (abort, CAL C: dy is #<dy_off> mm, outside 1 to 400 - that is not a pose anywhere near the puck.)
    o12 endif
    o13 if [#<depth> LE 1.0 OR #<depth> GT 400.0]
      (abort, CAL C: depth below the top is #<depth> mm, outside 1 to 400 - that is not a pose anywhere near the puck.)
    o13 endif
    o14 if [#<dx_off> GE 0]
      (abort, CAL C: the tip is not in FRONT of the puck - X offset must be negative so the probe drives toward centre in +X.)
    o14 endif
    #3061 = #<dx_off>
    #3058 = #<dy_off>
    #3060 = #<depth>
    #3059 = 0
    (PRINT, CAL C: reference captured from your jog - X offset #3061 mm, dy off centre #3058 mm, depth below top #3060 mm.)
  o10 else
    o15 if [#3058 EQ 0]
      (abort, CAL C: no C reference. Press SET C REF, jog the tip into place, then press StartC.)
    o15 endif
  o10 endif

  (--- shared setup, GLOBAL so the file-level helper can read it -----------)
  #<_cc_cy>    = #<cy>
  #<_cc_top>   = #<top>
  #<_cc_xr>    = [#<cx> + #3061]
  #<_cc_zoff>  = #3060
  #<_cc_safe>  = #<safe>
  #<_cc_reach> = 30.0    (max +X probe travel from the taught standoff)
  (rotary traverse: A and C cap at 30 deg/s = 1800 deg/min, so 5x on 600)
  (would only be clamped. Operator 2026-08-03: run the rotaries at 1200.)
  #<_cc_frot>  = 1200.0
  #<_cc_fpr>   = 100.0
  #<_cc_fla>   = 10.0
  (non-probing traverse 5x faster -- operator 2026-08-03. X/Y allow 12000)
  (mm/min and Z 10158, so 2500 is well inside the axis limits.)
  #<_cc_ftr>   = 2500.0
  (the protective descent is 1 in now, not ~107 mm, so 5x costs nothing)
  (and saves ~30 s a pass -- operator 2026-08-03)
  #<_cc_fck>   = 1000.0
  (lift above the taught depth before travelling/rotating)
  #<_cc_lift>  = 25.4
  #<_cc_back>  = 1.0     (backoff before the latch, 1 mm is plenty)

  #<dy> = #3058

  (#3073 = did C ACTUALLY change - drives whether the puck needs re-finding)
  #3073 = 0


  M50 P0

  (FORCE THE START POSE -- see cal_a_zero. Every button now begins from the)
  (zero instead of assuming it is already there.)
  o<cal_goto_zero> call [#<cx>] [#<cy>] [#<top>]

  (UNBANKED CORRECTION FROM A DIED CYCLE -- UNDO IT BEFORE MEASURING.)
  (MOVED to AFTER the start pose is forced. It used to run FIRST, so its)
  (Z move was a ~350 mm descent from an unknown entry pose -- the exact)
  (thing the doctrine ten lines below forbids. Audit 2026-08-03.)
  (Banking makes the parameter file the zero and clears #3070, so #3070 is 0 at)
  (the start of every healthy cycle. A non-zero value means the previous run)
  (applied a rotation and then died before banking it -- an abort stops)
  (everything after it, so the revert path never ran. On 2026-08-03 a clamped)
  (1.000 deg bite was left in the head that way, the next cycle measured the)
  (0.2235 deg residual from it, and banking wrote the SUM as if all of it had)
  (been verified. Put the head back first, then measure from the real zero.)
  o8 if [#3070 NE 0]
    G90
    G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F[#<_cc_ftr>]
    G91
    G1 C[0 - #3070] F[#<_cc_frot>]
    G90
    (PRINT, CAL C: #3070 was #3070 deg - an unbanked correction from a cycle that died. Rotated back before measuring.)
    #3070 = 0
  o8 endif

  (X FIRST, THEN Y. Combined they move diagonally, which crosses the puck.)
  (X alone steps in front of it; only then is the big Y swing off the puck.)
  G90
  G1 X[#<cx> + #3061] F[#<_cc_ftr>]
  G1 Y[#<cy> + #<dy>] F[#<_cc_ftr>]

  M64 P3
  G4 P1.5

  (=== BEFORE: -45 at the taught Y, then +45 at the mirrored Y ============)
  o<cc_probe> call [[#3069 - 45]] [#<dy>]
  #<x_neg_b> = #<_cc_tx>
  o<cc_probe> call [[#3069 + 45]] [0 - #<dy>]
  #<x_pos_b> = #<_cc_tx>
  #<dx_b> = [#<x_pos_b> - #<x_neg_b>]
  #3055 = #<dx_b>
  (PRINT, CAL C BEFORE: x at -45 = #<x_neg_b>, x at +45 = #<x_pos_b>, DELTA X = #<dx_b>)

  (=== correct: phi = asin of [-dX / 2dy] =================================)
  (dy KEEPS ITS SIGN. dX = -2 * dy * sin phi, so dy must enter signed:)
  (with ABS, a jog to NEGATIVE dy flipped phi and C rotated the wrong way by)
  (the full amount, doubling the error instead of removing it. The recheck)
  (would have caught it, but only after swinging the head the wrong way.)
  (Found by inspection 2026-08-03, never run on the machine.)
  #<ratio> = [[0 - #<dx_b>] / [2 * #<dy>]]
  o220 if [ABS[#<ratio>] GE 1.0]
    G90
    M65 P3
  (start AND end of every button is the ZERO -- operator 2026-08-03. That)
  (covers the ABORT paths too: a cycle dying at a standoff is exactly what)
  (made the next button's assumptions wrong.)
  o<cal_goto_zero> call [#<cx>] [#<cy>] [#<top>]
    M50 P1
    (abort, CAL C: dX exceeds twice the taught offset - the geometry does not fit the model, refusing to rotate C.)
  o220 endif
  #<phi> = ASIN[#<ratio>]

  (ABORT above 5 deg -- same rule as A: past 5 deg it is a real fault, not a)
  (misalignment, and nibbling would only hide it.)
  o228 if [ABS[#<phi>] GT 5.0]
    G90
    G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F[#<_cc_ftr>]
    M65 P3
  (start AND end of every button is the ZERO -- operator 2026-08-03. That)
  (covers the ABORT paths too: a cycle dying at a standoff is exactly what)
  (made the next button's assumptions wrong.)
  o<cal_goto_zero> call [#<cx>] [#<cy>] [#<top>]
    M50 P1
    (abort, CAL C: computed correction #<phi> deg is over 5 deg. That is a real error, not a misalignment - check the taught reference and the C sign before running this again.)
  o228 endif

  (CLAMP to 1 deg, do NOT abort -- operator 2026-08-03, same rule as A. Take)
  (one 1 deg bite in the computed direction and let the re-probe judge it.)
  #<cclamp> = 0
  o230 if [#<phi> GT 1.0]
    #<phi> = 1.0
    #<cclamp> = 1
  o230 endif
  o231 if [#<phi> LT -1.0]
    #<phi> = -1.0
    #<cclamp> = 1
  o231 endif
  o232 if [#<cclamp> EQ 1]
    (PRINT, CAL C: computed correction exceeded 1 deg - clamped to #<phi> deg. Applying one bite and re-measuring.)
  o232 endif

  (assigned AFTER the clamp, so it is the angle actually applied)
  #3057 = #<phi>
  (PRINT, CAL C: rotating C by #<phi> deg)

  G90
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F[#<_cc_ftr>]
  G91
  G1 C#<phi> F[#<_cc_frot>]
  G90
  #3070 = [#3070 + #<phi>]

  (=== AFTER: the same pair again =========================================)
  o<cc_probe> call [[#3069 - 45]] [#<dy>]
  #<x_neg_a> = #<_cc_tx>
  o<cc_probe> call [[#3069 + 45]] [0 - #<dy>]
  #<x_pos_a> = #<_cc_tx>
  #<dx_a> = [#<x_pos_a> - #<x_neg_a>]
  #3056 = #<dx_a>
  (PRINT, CAL C AFTER: x at -45 = #<x_neg_a>, x at +45 = #<x_pos_a>, DELTA X = #<dx_a>)

  (=== VERDICT + ANNEAL, at the standoff and clear of the puck ===========)
  (ORDER MATTERS AND WAS WRONG HERE: this block used to park and call)
  (cal_goto_zero BEFORE judging, so the revert rotation happened after the)
  (machine had already returned to zero -- swinging C at 5 mm above the puck,)
  (and leaving the routine NOT at the zero it had just gone to. A had it the)
  (right way round. Judge and adjust at the standoff, park once, afterwards.)

  (Operator 2026-08-03: if the full correction does not improve, RESET first,)
  (then try a quarter and re-measure. If both fail, nothing is banked.)
  o240 if [ABS[#<dx_a>] LT ABS[#<dx_b>]]
    #3073 = 1
    (PRINT, CAL C OK: dX #<dx_b> -> #<dx_a> mm, C moved #<phi> deg. KEPT.)
    (DEBUG, CAL C: dX #<dx_b> to #<dx_a> mm, C corrected #<phi> deg - KEPT)
  o240 else
    (RESET to the starting angle FIRST -- a quarter measured from the overshot)
    (position is not a quarter of the original correction.)
    (RISE CLEAR BEFORE ROTATING. cc_probe leaves the tip 1.0 mm off the puck)
    (face, and a C rotation moves it tangentially by dy times sin phi --)
    (3.4 mm per degree, essentially straight at the puck. The full)
    (correction rises first for this reason; these did not, and were safe)
    (only by an arithmetic coincidence a deeper re-teach would break.)
    (Audit 2026-08-03.)
    G90
    G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F[#<_cc_ftr>]
    G91
    G1 C[0 - #<phi>] F[#<_cc_frot>]
    G90
    #3070 = [#3070 - #<phi>]

    #<qtr> = [#<phi> / 4]
    G91
    G1 C#<qtr> F[#<_cc_frot>]
    G90
    #3070 = [#3070 + #<qtr>]
    (PRINT, CAL C: #<phi> deg did not improve dX #<dx_b> -> #<dx_a>. Reset, and trying a quarter: #<qtr> deg.)

    (re-measure the SAME pair, same tilts, same Y mirror, so the numbers stay)
    (comparable to dx_b)
    o<cc_probe> call [[#3069 - 45]] [#<dy>]
    #<x_neg_q> = #<_cc_tx>
    o<cc_probe> call [[#3069 + 45]] [0 - #<dy>]
    #<x_pos_q> = #<_cc_tx>
    #<dx_q> = [#<x_pos_q> - #<x_neg_q>]
    #3056 = #<dx_q>
    (PRINT, CAL C QUARTER: x at -45 = #<x_neg_q>, x at +45 = #<x_pos_q>, DELTA X = #<dx_q>)

    o250 if [ABS[#<dx_q>] LT ABS[#<dx_b>]]
      #3057 = #<qtr>
      #3073 = 1
      (PRINT, CAL C OK on the quarter: dX #<dx_b> -> #<dx_q> mm, C moved #<qtr> deg. KEPT.)
      (DEBUG, CAL C: quarter kept - dX #<dx_b> to #<dx_q> mm, C corrected #<qtr> deg)
    o250 else
      G90
      G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F[#<_cc_ftr>]
      G91
      G1 C[0 - #<qtr>] F[#<_cc_frot>]
      G90
      #3070 = [#3070 - #<qtr>]
      #3057 = 0
      #3073 = 0
      (PRINT, CAL C DISCARDED: neither #<phi> deg [dX #<dx_a>] nor a quarter #<qtr> deg [dX #<dx_q>] beat #<dx_b> mm. C is exactly where it started, nothing banked, puck re-find skipped.)
      (DEBUG, CAL C DISCARDED: full and quarter both failed - C unchanged)
    o250 endif
  o240 endif

  (=== park: puck down, end on the ZERO -- start AND end of every button ===)
  G90
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F[#<_cc_ftr>]
  M65 P3
  G4 P1.0
  o<cal_goto_zero> call [#<cx>] [#<cy>] [#<top>]
  M50 P1

o<cal_c_zero> endsub

M2 (end program)
